# Local integration API (OpenClaw / Inwestor)

LibreWallet exposes portfolio data to **local tools only**.

## Preferred: agent feed (rich)

Native macOS writes atomically:

`~/Library/Application Support/LibreWallet/agent-feed.json`

Same JSON via:

`GET http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/agent-feed`

Includes `positions[]` (qty, cost, value, P/L), `cash[]` per portfolio/currency, aggregates, and quote freshness (`quotesAgeMinutes`, `staleSymbols`, `missingQuotes`). No account numbers / `externalId` / notes.

File works even if HTTP is down (as long as feed was published recently). HTTP rebuilds + rewrites the file on each GET.

## Legacy endpoints (still supported)

| Method | Path | Behavior |
|--------|------|----------|
| `GET` | `/api/health` | `{ ok, service, version, source? }` |
| `GET` | `/api/holdings` | Metadata-only instruments (compat) |
| `GET` | `/api/portfolio` | Aggregates + metadata holdings (compat) |
| `POST` | `/api/holdings` | Web cache update; macOS no-op |
| `POST` | `/api/quotes` | macOS: refresh store quotes + republish feed |

## Runtime

1. **Native macOS** — `LocalIntegrationServer` on `127.0.0.1:8787` + live SwiftData; `AgentFeedPublisher` on save / launch / quote refresh.
2. **Web / `server.js`** — in-memory holdings cache only (no agent-feed file).

Prefer native app as source of truth. Only one process can bind `:8787`.

## Security

- Bind `127.0.0.1` only.
- No auth on loopback.
- Do not use `0.0.0.0` without understanding LAN exposure.
